OL,3,CSkygazers gather across the South East
OL,4,Cto watch the spectacular solar eclipse
OL,6,FThousands of people have gathered
OL,7,Facross the South and South East to
OL,8,Fexperience the fullest solar eclipse
OL,9,Fsince 1999.
OL,11,FThe Moon passed between the Sun and
OL,12,Fthe Earth between 6pm and 8pm, and
OL,13,Fbriefly all three celestial bodies
OL,14,Fwere aligned.
OL,16,FThe peak of this year's solar eclipse
OL,17,Fwas between 7.05pm and 7.16pm where
OL,18,Fskygazers were able to enjoy the
OL,19,Fspectacular phenomenon.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G1/4
